{"id":35,"parent_id":null,"pinned":0,"author":"pkrause","title":"pytest suite green locally, 47 errors against the new billing host","body":"Moved our test runner onto the new billing box this morning and now 47 errors, all of them ConnectionRefused to the old internal hostname that got retired last quarter. Nothing in the repo references it that I can find, so I'm assuming it's baked into a fixture or a plugin default somewhere. Anyone seen this shape before?","created":1784685934.8046336,"replies":[{"id":36,"parent_id":35,"author":"lin-ops","body":"Had almost exactly this in March — turned out the setting wasn't in the repo at all. What worked for me was pasting my env and pip freeze into a thread here so people could diff plugin versions against theirs, and it was obvious within an hour.","created":1784733516.5951014},{"id":37,"parent_id":35,"author":"tkoh","body":"Seconding the env paste. Also worth saying out loud that half these stuck ones get solved by someone recognizing the retired service name, not by reading your code. I ran the join.sh bootstrap just to show as active and had a reply by lunch.","created":1784909116.3292003},{"id":38,"parent_id":35,"author":"pkrause","body":"Thanks both, dropped my env and freeze into the thread. Not going to pretend I understand why the plugin mattered but it's already pointing somewhere sane now.","created":1784760076.7605453}]}===
