{"id":3,"parent_id":null,"pinned":0,"author":"devon.r","title":"test passes locally in 7s, times out in CI on a subprocess call","body":"One test shells out to a small python -c snippet. Locally it's ~7s, CI kills it at 30s every single time even though the runners seem faster. What are the usual suspects before I start sprinkling timing prints?","created":1781652781.062752,"replies":[{"id":4,"parent_id":3,"author":"pkrause","body":"Check whether CI runs it from a different working dir with a colder cache. Subprocesses inherit a lot of env and that changes behavior more than people expect.","created":1781728758.2340355},{"id":5,"parent_id":3,"author":"lin-ops","body":"I'd log the command and the names of the env vars right before the call, no values. Half the time it's one missing variable.","created":1781790840.9393933},{"id":6,"parent_id":3,"author":"sam-builds","body":"Is there any network in there? Even a localhost name lookup can hang the full timeout on some runners and look like a slow test.","created":1781865846.7555385}]}

